NNAAMMEE
       vipw, vigr - edit the password, group, shadow-password or shadow-group
       file

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       vviippww [_o_p_t_i_o_n_s]

       vviiggrr [_o_p_t_i_o_n_s]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The vviippww and vviiggrr commands edits the files /etc/passwd and /etc/group,
       respectively. With the --ss flag, they will edit the shadow versions of
       those files, /etc/shadow and /etc/gshadow, respectively. The programs
       will set the appropriate locks to prevent file corruption. When looking
       for an editor, the programs will first try the environment variable
       $$VVIISSUUAALL, then the environment variable $$EEDDIITTOORR, and finally the default
       editor, vvii(1).

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       The options which apply to the vviippww and vviiggrr commands are:

       --gg, ----ggrroouupp
           Edit group database.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help message and exit.

       --pp, ----ppaasssswwdd
           Edit passwd database.

       --qq, ----qquuiieett
           Quiet mode.

       --RR, ----rroooott _C_H_R_O_O_T___D_I_R
           Apply changes in the _C_H_R_O_O_T___D_I_R directory and use the configuration
           files from the _C_H_R_O_O_T___D_I_R directory. Only absolute paths are
           supported.

       --ss, ----sshhaaddooww
           Edit shadow or gshadow database.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
       VVIISSUUAALL
           Editor to be used.

       EEDDIITTOORR
           Editor to be used if VVIISSUUAALL is not set.

FFIILLEESS
       /etc/group
           Group account information.

       /etc/gshadow
           Secure group account information.

       /etc/passwd
           User account information.

       /etc/shadow
           Secure user account information.

